## What I annotated

The app is *CompetencyHub* (Vite + React + shadcn, single route with two view states):

| Screen / component | Hints |
|---|---|
| **Header / footer** (`Index.tsx`) | `nav.models`, `nav.analytics`, three `footer.*` links |
| **Browse screen** | `home.stats` collection (3), `models.filters` region, `models.search.query` input, `models.filter.department` select + options, `models.grid` collection (5), `models.grid.empty` |
| **Model detail** | `model.detail.header` region, back/export/share/save, title/department/count observables |
| **Metrics** | coverage, avg level, critical-path & risk-gap counts, two badge collections, both alerts |
| **Graph** (`CompetencyNode`) | `graph` collection with 6 nodes; per node: enabled toggle, category/critical/gap badges, level readout, **5 level buttons**, weight slider + display |
| **Simulation** | `simulation.scenarios` tab collection (3), `simulation.adjustments` collection (4 categories × slider+display pairs), run/reset |
| **Template library** | `templates.list` collection (5), per-item metadata + apply action, save-current |
| **404 + toast** | `notFound.*`; `toast`/`toast.title`/`toast.message`/`toast.close` in the shared toaster |

**Namespaces:** `nav.*`, `footer.*`, `home.stats.*`, `models.*`, `model.detail.*`, `metrics.*`, `graph.*`, `simulation.*`, `templates.*`, `toast.*`, `notFound.*`.

## Verification beyond the linter

The linter can't see DOM ancestry or runtime ids, so I wrote a temporary vitest harness (since deleted) that rendered every screen and asserted **zero duplicate ids** and **zero orphaned `.item.` ids** on the browse screen, the detail screen, after a tab switch, after a toast, and in the empty state. This confirmed the two things I couldn't take on faith:

- **ReactFlow nodes really land inside the `graph` collection** — they're portal-ish and rendered by the library, so I verified all 6 `graph.item.*` ids resolve under the container.
- **`simulation.adjustments` is mounted exactly once.** It's rendered inside *every* `TabsContent`, which would have meant 3 duplicate copies. I read the Radix source (`children: present && children`) and confirmed inactive tabs render nothing.

## Notes

- **No prop-widening was needed** — every shadcn component already spreads `...props`.
- **Behavior is provably unchanged.** I diffed against the pristine copy in `web_applications/`: stripping all `data-semtag-*` attributes makes 9 of 10 files byte-identical to the original modulo whitespace. The tenth (`toaster.tsx`) differs only by parentheses added around `&&` JSX during reformatting.
- **The 6 `flat-id` INFOs are expected** — they're top-level region/collection ids (`graph`, `metrics`, `simulation`, `templates`, `toast`, `notFound`), which the spec explicitly permits.
- **Pre-existing lint failures:** `npm run lint` reports 3 errors + 7 warnings. These are **not mine** — I linted the pristine original and the file list is byte-identical. All are shadcn/tailwind boilerplate (`no-empty-object-type`, `no-require-imports`); none of the 10 files I touched produce any finding.

**Deliberately left unhinted:** keyword badges on model/template cards (~35 elements of low value), the model description paragraphs (long text), the decorative chevron button, ReactFlow's Controls/MiniMap/edges, the unused `NavLink.tsx` dead code, and the inert `<Sonner />` toaster.

One thing worth flagging: I ran `npm ci` to install dependencies, which weren't present. That's the only change outside `src/`.

